ce, which is about 1.2x cover. H1 orders rose 11% year on year, led by utility and data-centre customers, and cancellations stayed below 1%.\n- **Run-rate:** Quarterly revenue was C$905M in 2025Q3, C$960M in 2025Q4, C$980M in 2026Q1 and C$890M in 2026Q2 (n3.d3). The 2026Q2 dip was an outage, not a demand problem. C$4.2B for 2027 needs about C$1.05B a quarter, roughly 7% above the 2026Q1 level of C$980M. That is plausible with an 11% rise in orders.\n- **Operations:** Halbrook builds all of Voltaris's large power transformers. A fire in the coil-winding hall shut it for nine weeks in Q2 (n2.d5). It restarted in August at full capacity (n2.d7), and the delayed orders are to be delivered under a recovery plan. The delayed orders were probably deferred rather than lost, so some of that revenue should move into H2 2026 and 2027.\n- **Risks:** Because Halbrook is the only source of large transformers, any further stoppage there would hit 2027 directly. The backlog also takes time to convert, and \"covers\" is management's own claim. The industry data, which n3 reads as pointing below guidance (n3.r1), is a separate judgment from mine, and n1 will have to weigh the two.","ttft_ms":2463,"type":"result","duration_ms":49483,"uuid":"eff00f11-cd08-45a0-bb33-631916fedbdc","ttft_stream_ms":1364,"time_to_request_ms":205,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":20,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":18,"tool_pool_refresh":6,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":12,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":12,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":6,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":11,"client_creation":10,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":101,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"pro